      "message": "Should also check this for `var` initializers.\n\nIn fact, since all operands to all valid root-block instructions must always be const/override, you could just do this check before the `tint::Switch` instead of in each switch-case block.\n\nAlthough I see now that the lambda also adds the instruction result to `pipeline_evaluatable`, which you don\u0027t want to do for `var` instructions. Maybe do the operand check before the switch and then add to pipeline_evaluatable inside the cases (don\u0027t need to check for instruction results since all of these instructions have them)?",
